Malik, 18 – Stomach Virus

“I got a stomach virus during the school year and it messed me up more than I thought it would. It started late at night and by the next morning I felt terrible. I couldn’t eat anything and even moving around made me feel worse. I had to stay home for a couple days because there was no way I could go to school like that.

At first I didn’t think about how easy it could spread, but my family kept reminding me to wash my hands and not touch stuff around the house too much. That actually made me more aware of how stuff like that spreads.

The hardest part was just waiting it out. There wasn’t much I could do except rest and stay hydrated. After it passed, I was still really tired, which I didn’t expect.

Advice:

Wash your hands a lot to avoid spreading it
Stay home until you’re fully better
Don’t rush back into normal activities
Drink small amounts of water often

Now I’m way more careful about hygiene because I don’t want to go through that again or cause someone else to.”
